---
description: Directory ownership and the handoff report — applies when writing any source file
globs: ["src/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Parallel agents fail on write conflicts long before they fail on reasoning.
Ownership is by **directory**, not by feature description.

| Area | Owner | Everyone else |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `src/design-system/` | design system | read-only — request via ADR |
| `src/components/`, `src/patterns/` | design system | read-only — request additions |
| `src/lib/domain/`, `src/lib/simulation/` | platform | read-only |
| `src/lib/i18n/locales/*.json` | **append-only for everyone** | add keys, never edit another agent's |
| `src/features/<role>/` | that role's agent | hands off |
| `tools/`, `context/`, `eslint-rules/` | harness | propose, don't silently edit |

**Locale files are the one shared write surface.** Namespace your keys by screen
(`client.overview.heroTitle`, not `heroTitle`) and add to **both** `en.json` and
`id.json` — `npm run verify:i18n` fails on parity drift.

**Need something from a directory you don't own?** Ask for it, or write against
the documented contract in `src/components/contracts.ts` and flag the
dependency. Do not reach in.

## Before you start

- Check `npm run trace` — is your requirement already claimed by a file?
- Confirm you own the directory you are about to write to.

## When you finish

Report in this shape — it is what the next agent needs and nothing more:

```
Requirement(s):  FR-10, FR-15
Files:           src/features/client/Overview.tsx (+3)
Verify:          pass
Not done:        empty state for the maintenance timeline — needs the
                 work-order shape from the platform agent
Decisions:       used a tinted severity chip rather than a filled badge
Open questions:  none
```

**"Not done" is the most valuable line.** Silence there is read as completeness,
and that is how a sprint arrives at a demo with three broken screens nobody
flagged.
